<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="lt">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>{% block title %}Mokesčių Sufleris{% endblock %}</title>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Open+Sans:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;0,700;1,400&family=Roboto+Mono:wght@400&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="build/app.css">
</head>
<body>
    {#
        "Content concept" shell — a SEPARATE template from base.html.twig
        on purpose (see templates/base.html.twig's own header comment).
        That one is the DS-admin documentation site's own chrome
        (Foundations/Components sidebar, "Kodas" panels, DialKit widget);
        this one is a live template for what an actual Mokesčių Sufleris
        product page looks like — different sidebar content, different
        topbar, an AI assistant panel, a real multi-column footer. They
        share nothing structurally, so there's no shell-switcher/DialKit
        widget here and this page doesn't appear in the DS-admin's own
        "Pages / Templates" nav (deliberately kept standalone for now).

        Figma reference: node 5669:1509 ("Side Ai Veldy - compact").
        Colors/spacing/type come from our own DS tokens (_variables.scss,
        _theme.scss), not the reference's own raw values.

        `sidebarCollapsed` is shared state for every included partial
        below (sidebar, topbar) since Alpine scope flows down through
        `{% include %}` the same as through nested HTML — persisted like
        every other sticky UI preference in this project (ds-shell,
        ds-sidebar-sections, ds-show-code, ...).
    #}
    <div class="content-shell" x-data="contentShellState()" :class="{ 'is-sidebar-collapsed': sidebarCollapsed }">
        {% include "partials/_content-sidebar.html.twig" %}

        <div class="content-shell__main">
            {% include "partials/_content-topbar.html.twig" %}

            {#
                Sidebar + topbar are the only fixed chrome — content, the
                AI panel, AND the footer all scroll together as one
                region below the topbar (the footer is tall enough on
                its own that giving it a fixed flex slot alongside the
                content row squeezed the row down to almost nothing).
            #}
            <div class="content-shell__scroll">
                <div class="content-shell__body">
                    <main class="content-shell__content">
                        {% block content %}{% endblock %}
                    </main>

                    {% include "partials/_ai-panel.html.twig" %}
                </div>

                {% include "partials/_content-footer.html.twig" %}
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    {% block javascripts %}
        <script src="build/runtime.js"></script>
        <script src="build/app.js"></script>
    {% endblock %}
</body>
</html>
